  "summary": "Claire Lomas, a 44-year-old charity campaigner who became famous for completing marathons in a bionic suit after being paralyzed in a horse riding accident, has died following an accident in Jordan on August 22. Lomas was paralyzed from the chest down in 2007 after being thrown from her horse at the Osberton Horse Trials, suffering severe injuries including a broken neck and back. She gained international attention for completing the 2012 London Marathon in 17 days wearing her bionic suit and was later chosen to light the Paralympic cauldron in Trafalgar Square. Throughout her campaigning career, she raised nearly £1 million for charity through various events, including completing the Great North Run while pregnant in 2016. Her family has requested privacy during their time of grief."
